# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/settings.json
*.iml

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
*.env

# Claude Code
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/temp/
.claude/ralph-loop.local.md
# Shared design rules are committed although a global `*.local.md` ignore would hide them
# (that is how the tier rules went missing while their tests were committed). Personal hookify rules stay local.
!.claude/hookify.design-*.local.md
# security-guidance plugin: per-developer overrides (project files stay committed)
.claude/claude-security-guidance.local.md
.claude/security-patterns.local.yaml
.claude/security-patterns.local.yml
.claude/security-patterns.local.json
# Subagent `memory:` notes are written from whatever project the agent worked on.
# Durable knowledge is promoted through /promote-lessons; raw notes are never committed.
.claude/agent-memory/
.claude/agent-memory-local/

# Runtime state and retired logging systems — never commit prompt logs or generated state
# legacy location of hook state (now .git/claude-state/, outside the working tree)
.claude/state/
blackbox/
.claude/smart-suggest.jsonl
CLAUDE.local.md

# Credentials & secrets
*-credentials.json
*-credentials-*.json
sheets-mcp-credentials.json

# Miscellaneous
*.log
# Hook runtime audit logs (already covered by *.log above; listed explicitly for
# discoverability) — written by output-secrets-scanner.sh, output-llm-quota-guard.sh,
# stopfailure-api-error-notice.sh, and session-mcp-governance.sh.
.claude/*-detected.log
*.swp
.buildlog/
.history

